    The phone's own look, and no bar: an add-on has one screen, which draws its
    own title so that it can be laid out with the rest of the text rather than
    above it. DayNight has no NoActionBar variant of its own, hence the two
    items.
-->
<resources>
    <style name="Theme.Plugin" parent="@android:style/Theme.DeviceDefault.DayNight">
        <item name="android:windowActionBar">false</item>
        <item name="android:windowNoTitle">true</item>
    </style>
</resources>
